Address protocol #32 review: scope heard, pin the ask, peer-free matching, stale vectors

- Ask on each new control connection is now MUST; the ask conditions
  state the closed audio transport and a present page (not navigating).
- lifecycle.py latches heard only for the recording's own callGeneration,
  so another call's heard cannot arm restore, OTHERS_GONE_GRACE or the ask.
  New case pins it; ask-waits gains a navigating row and a call-B row.
- callGeneration is a browser-generated unguessable ID; lost recordings
  match by (tabId, callGeneration) across all control peers. The lost call
  is recording: Record all skips it (expect.manual false), manual Record
  after Stop is an ordinary Start. Seeded recordings start unlatched
  (heardSeen); new heard-earlier and earlier-peer auto-start cases.
- The extension manual runner checks wire acceptance for seeded cases,
  since the app registry is invisible to the extension.
- SPEC.md makes the PCM_STALE_AFTER >= comparison normative; new
  stale-watchdog.json with an independent oracle and mutant tests.

